.TH "ELEMENT.TOUCHEND_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Element.touchend_event \- Element: touchend event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[CR]touchend\f[R] event fires when one or more touch points are
removed from the touch surface.
Remember that it is possible to get a \f[CR]touchcancel\f[R] event
instead.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqtouchend\(dq, (event) => { })

ontouchend = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]TouchEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
Code samples for those events are available on the dedicated page: Touch
events.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Touch events
